---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import Cta from '../../components/Cta.astro';
import Disclosure from '../../components/Disclosure.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import nordvpn from '../../data/nordvpn.js';
import competitors from '../../data/competitors.js';
import { site, legal } from '../../config.js';

const n = nordvpn;
const t = n.pricing.tiers;

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How much does NordVPN cost per month?', a: `It depends on the term. Basic is $${t[0].monthly} billed monthly, $${t[0].yearly} a month on an annual plan, or $${t[0].twoYear} a month on the two-year plan. Complete is $${t[1].twoYear} and Prime is $${t[2].twoYear} on the same two-year term.` },
  { q: 'Why is the two-year plan billed for 27 months?', a: `Because the current promotion includes three extra months on top of the 24-month term. You pay $${t[0].twoYearTotal} once and get ${t[0].twoYearMonths} months of service, which is what produces the $${t[0].twoYear}-a-month equivalent.` },
  { q: 'What does NordVPN cost at renewal?', a: `Basic renews at roughly $139.08 a year (about $11.59 a month), Complete at roughly $219.48 a year, and Prime at roughly $296.28 a year. The introductory rate applies only to the first term.` },
  { q: 'Is NordVPN more expensive than its rivals?', a: `On the two-year Basic plan at $${t[0].twoYear} a month, it sits above budget rivals and below ExpressVPN. It is not the cheapest premium VPN, and it does not pretend to be.` },
  { q: 'Does NordVPN offer refunds?', a: `${n.pricing.guarantee} on every plan, processed through live chat. Subscriptions bought through the App Store or Google Play follow that store's rules instead.` },
  { q: 'Can I pay monthly and cancel anytime?', a: `Yes. The monthly Basic plan is $${t[0].monthly} and can be cancelled at any time, but there is no partial refund on longer terms once the ${n.pricing.guarantee.split(' ')[0]}-day window closes.` },
  { q: 'Is NordVPN cheaper in some countries?', a: 'Yes. Pricing varies by country and currency, and the promotional percentage differs by market. Some markets see meaningfully lower local prices, though payment-method checks increasingly limit cross-region signups.' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Product',
  name: 'NordVPN',
  brand: { '@type': 'Brand', name: 'NordVPN' },
  offers: t.map((tier) => ({
    '@type': 'Offer',
    name: `NordVPN ${tier.name} (2-year)`,
    price: String(tier.twoYear),
    priceCurrency: 'USD',
    availability: 'https://schema.org/InStock',
  })),
  aggregateRating: { '@type': 'AggregateRating', ratingValue: String(n.score.overall), reviewCount: '1', bestRating: '5' },
};
---
<Base
  title="NordVPN pricing 2026: every plan and term"
  description={`Full NordVPN pricing breakdown for 2026. Basic $${t[0].twoYear}/mo, Complete $${t[1].twoYear}/mo, Prime $${t[2].twoYear}/mo on two-year terms. Monthly and annual prices, renewal costs, and which tier to buy.`}
  slug="/pricing/nordvpn-pricing"
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Crumbs items={[{ label: 'Pricing', href: '/pricing/nordvpn-pricing' }]} />

    <article class="narrow">
      <p class="count">US-store prices &middot; verified {new Date(site.factsVerifiedOn).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' })}</p>
      <h1>NordVPN pricing explained: every plan and every term</h1>
      <p class="hub-intro">NordVPN's pricing looks simple and is not. Three tiers, three terms, a promotion that adds three months, and a renewal price roughly triple the headline. Here is all of it in one place, including the part the marketing does not lead with.</p>

      <Disclosure variant="long" />

      <h2 id="table">The full price table</h2>
      <div class="tablewrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Plan</th><th>Monthly</th><th>1 year</th><th>2 years</th><th>2-year total</th><th>Renewal</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {t.map((tier) => (
              <tr>
                <td><strong>{tier.name}</strong></td>
                <td class="num">${tier.monthly}</td>
                <td class="num">${tier.yearly}</td>
                <td class="num hi">${tier.twoYear}</td>
                <td class="num">${tier.twoYearTotal}</td>
                <td>{tier.renewal}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>{n.pricing.note}</p>

      <div class="note">
        <strong>Renewal pricing is the single most important number on this page.</strong>
        The $3.49 headline is an introductory rate. Basic renews at roughly $139.08 a year and Complete at roughly $219.48. NordVPN sends an email before charging, but the email is easy to miss and the charge is not. Set a calendar reminder for two weeks before your renewal date.
      </div>

      <Cta slug="pricing-page" title={`Basic two-year: $${t[0].twoYear}/month`} body={`$${t[0].twoYearTotal} for ${t[0].twoYearMonths} months including three extra. ${n.pricing.guarantee}.`} />

      <h2 id="tiers">What each tier actually includes</h2>
      {t.map((tier) => (
        <>
          <h3>{tier.name} &mdash; ${tier.twoYear}/month on two years</h3>
          <p>{tier.pitch}</p>
          {tier.extras.length > 0
            ? <ul>{tier.extras.map((e) => <li>{e}</li>)}</ul>
            : <p><strong>Includes:</strong> the full VPN with {n.network.servers} servers in {n.network.countries} countries, {n.devices.simultaneous} simultaneous connections, kill switch, split tunnelling, Threat Protection and Meshnet.</p>}
          <p><strong>Best for:</strong> {tier.bestFor}</p>
        </>
      ))}

      <h2 id="hidden">The costs people miss</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Renewal at roughly triple the introductory rate.</strong> Covered above, and the biggest surprise for new subscribers.</li>
        <li><strong>Dedicated IP is a separate paid add-on.</strong> Available in 28+ countries, priced per year on top of your subscription.</li>
        <li><strong>Threat Protection Pro requires the Complete tier.</strong> The Basic plan includes standard Threat Protection but not the anti-malware file scanning.</li>
        <li><strong>The full two-year term is paid upfront.</strong> ${t[0].twoYearTotal} at purchase, with no partial refunds after the guarantee window closes.</li>
        <li><strong>App Store and Google Play purchases follow store refund rules.</strong> Buy direct from NordVPN if the money-back guarantee matters to you.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="compare">How the price compares</h2>
      <div class="tablewrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th>Lowest price</th><th>Term</th><th>Devices</th><th>Countries</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="hi"><strong>NordVPN Basic</strong></td><td class="num">${t[0].twoYear}/mo</td><td>2 years</td><td>{n.devices.simultaneous}</td><td>{n.network.countries}</td></tr>
            {competitors.slice(0, 8).map((c) => (
              <tr>
                <td><a href={`/compare/nordvpn-vs-${c.id}`}>{c.name}</a></td>
                <td class="num">{c.bestPrice}</td>
                <td>{c.bestPriceNote}</td>
                <td>{c.devices}</td>
                <td>{c.countries}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>NordVPN is not the cheapest and does not claim to be. It sits above the budget tier and below ExpressVPN, and the argument for it is that you are buying the largest network, the fastest protocol and the strongest unblocking record rather than the lowest number. See <a href="/pricing/nordvpn-pricing#tiers">the tier breakdown</a> or <a href="/compare">all comparisons</a>.</p>

      <h2 id="save">How to pay the least</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><strong>Buy the two-year Basic plan.</strong> At ${t[0].twoYear} a month it is the cheapest NordVPN has ever been, and Basic includes the entire VPN.</li>
        <li><strong>Skip Complete unless you would pay for a password manager anyway.</strong> NordPass and 1 TB of NordLocker storage are the main additions. If you already use 1Password or Bitwarden, you are paying for things you do not need.</li>
        <li><strong>Set the renewal reminder immediately.</strong> Two weeks before the term ends, decide consciously rather than letting it auto-renew at roughly $139.</li>
        <li><strong>Use the guarantee to test.</strong> {n.pricing.guarantee} means you can verify it works on your network and with your streaming services before you are committed.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignore coupon sites.</strong> There is no code to enter. The discount applies automatically at checkout.</li>
      </ol>

      <Faq faqs={faqs} />

      <p class="disclosure" style="margin-top:2rem">{legal.specDisclaimer}</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
